---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Refunds — Sealshot"
  description="Sealshot's refund policy: 30 days, no questions required — and the app is free to use, so you can decide before paying."
>
  <section class="section wrap prose" aria-labelledby="refunds-title">
    <p class="kicker">Refunds</p>
    <h1 id="refunds-title">30 days, no questions required</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      If Sealshot isn't right for you, email
      <a href="mailto:support@seal-shot.com">support@seal-shot.com</a> within 30
      days of buying and we'll refund it in full.
    </p>

    <h2>Try it before you pay</h2>
    <p>
      Sealshot is <strong>free to use</strong>, with every feature unlocked and no
      account required. Most reasons for a refund are things using it would have
      shown you first, so we'd rather you did — and if you bought on day one,
      that's still no obstacle to a refund.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are handled by <a href="https://polar.sh" rel="nofollow">Polar</a>,
      our merchant of record, so the refund is processed by them and returns to
      the card you paid with. Email us, or reply to your Polar receipt — either
      reaches us. It usually completes within a few business days, depending on
      your bank.
    </p>
    <p>
      You don't have to give a reason. If something specific didn't work we'd
      genuinely like to hear it, because that's how the app gets better — but
      it's never a condition.
    </p>

    <h2>After a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing, mechanically: donations don't come with license keys, so there is
      nothing to revoke. <strong>Nothing you captured is deleted or locked</strong>
      and every feature keeps working — we'd only ask that you untick
      "I've donated" in Settings ▸ Support, on the same honor system the
      checkbox works by.
    </p>
    <p>
      Licenses bought before Sealshot became donation-supported are the one
      exception: refunding one revokes it, via a small public list that Sealshot
      downloads and checks <em>on your Mac</em>. Your license ID is never sent
      anywhere — see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Anything unclear before you buy? <a href="/support/">Ask us</a> — we'd
      rather answer a question than process a refund.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
